 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Both changes were made and are persisted. (1) Tag: opened Edit > Settings > General, typed 'bench' in the Tags field and clicked Add — a chip 'Remove \"bench\" tag' appeared — then clicked Save dashboard. (2) Time range: the top-bar picker already read \"Last 6 hours\"; in the save drawer I ticked the 'Update default time range' checkbox and confirmed Save, which produced the \"Dashboard saved\" alert. Persistence verified after a hard reload of the URL with NO query parameters: Edit > Settings > JSON Model (now version 3) shows \"tags\": [ \"bench\" ] and \"time\": { \"from\": \"now-6h\", \"to\": \"now\" } (timepicker is empty, so the default comes from the top-level time field), and the reloaded page renders \"Time range selected: Last 6 hours\" with both panels '{{v4}} Notes' (text \"Notes for run {{v4}}\") and '{{v4}} Availability' (Stat, value 62.8). One caveat: a stray Ctrl+F attempt got typed into the Monaco JSON editor, overwriting its local buffer, but I navigated away without clicking \"Save changes\" and afterwards re-verified the stored model reads correctly (tags bench, time now-6h/now), so nothing was corrupted.",
